            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "@justinmk \n\nI traced the CmdAtom path and the namespace discussion in #41387. My proposed approach would be to build on that existing namespace concept rather than introduce a separate ownership mechanism.\n\nAt a high level:\n\n1. Add an optional namespace to mapping and user-command definitions.\n2. Preserve that namespace when the mapping/command is resolved and executed.\n3. Propagate it into `CmdAtom` when the atom is constructed, following the existing pattern where optional CmdAtom fields are omitted when not applicable.\n4. For mappings, the namespace can be carried from the resolved `mapblock_T` into the CmdAtom creation path.\n5. For user commands, I’d trace the Ex command dispatch/resolution path first, since the current CmdAtom creation appears to start from the raw command line rather than directly from a `ucmd_T`.\n6. Add regression tests for direct mappings/commands, composite mappings, mapping → command cases, and unnamespaced definitions.\n\nOne thing I’d specifically handle is the single-subatom/composite case: when a mapping is unwrapped, its metadata still needs to be preserved, otherwise the namespace could be lost for simple mappings. I’d also make sure the namespace is captured as part of the deferred CmdAtom data rather than retaining a pointer to the mapping/command.\n\nI’d check #41414 for overlap first, then trace the remaining command-dispatch path and implement the smallest change consistent with the namespace model in #41387.",
